+# Resume results: what real agents did with a projected session
+
+Summary written 2026-10-20 by toolpath-author from the evidence files below. It states only what those files show. The evidence lives
+outside this repository (the fleet ops directory `~/.lobby/ops/goldens-session-2026-10-19/`); the files are named so a reader can check
+each line. Cells ran on toolpath `origin/wip/bdelanghe` at `f308ab5` or `c1e8cd9` as each file says, with nix-store agent binaries and a
+temp home, one model call per probe.
+
+## Method (same in every file)
+The probe asks, in one line, for facts only the recording's own history contains (the first file written, the replaced word, a
+sub-agent's count, or the facts the recording does have). Controls: a fresh session asked the same question answers `NONE`; a
+nonexistent session id is refused by the agent before any model call.
+
+## Own session: the agent's recording goes through toolpath and back into the same agent
+
+| agent (version) | probe reply | verdict | file |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| gemini-cli 0.47.0 | `notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 11` | loaded | there-and-back-gemini-opencode.md |
+| opencode 1.18.18 | `notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 10` | loaded | there-and-back-gemini-opencode.md |
+| codex-cli 0.162.1 | `notes.md \| wc -w notes.md \| 11` | loaded | there-and-back-codex-pi.md |
+| pi 0.84.3 | `notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 68` | loaded | there-and-back-codex-pi.md |
+| cursor-agent (from a Cursor IDE recording) | answered the history-only question correctly | loaded | there-and-back-cursor.md |
+
+Controls named in those files: fresh session `NONE`; bad id refused (gemini rc 42, opencode rc 1, codex rc 1 and pi rc 1 with no key in
+the environment). The codex and pi files report 4 model calls (gpt-5.4-mini) with their cost. The claude and copilot own-session cells are NOT in
+these files; the addendum's "7/7 own-session" count is not backed by a file I could read for those two.
+
+## Cross-agent: one agent's recording resumed by a different agent (cross-into-cursor-and-pi-opencode.md)
+
+| cell | verdict |
+|---|---|
+| claude-session -> cursor-agent | loaded (`notes.txt,other.txt \| first line of the notes`) |
+| codex -> cursor-agent | loaded (`notes.md \| wc -w notes.md \| 11`) |
+| pi -> cursor-agent | loaded (`notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 68`) |
+| copilot -> cursor-agent | loaded (`notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 16`) |
+| pi -> opencode | loaded (`notes.md \| scratch -> fixture \| 68`) |
+
+5 cells, 5 model calls, no error, no rate limit. The fresh-session controls were not repeated there; that file points to the two
+there-and-back files above.
+
+## What I could not find
+- **The "28/28 cross-agent" count.** No file I was pointed to holds 28 cross-agent cells. This summary shows these 5 cells (plus the own-session
+  rows). The earlier matrix runs are in `resume-matrix/` (`v5.sh`, `headless-gemini.sh`, `screens/v4-*.log` and `.cmd`); I did not
+  tabulate them, and v5.sh covers the opencode and gemini columns only. If 28/28 is meant to include them, the table is not yet in a file.
+- **Claude and copilot own-session cells** (see above).
+- **Driver and raw outputs:** `there-and-back/` (driver `tab.sh`, `.cmd`/`.out`/`.rc`/`.err` files, projected files). Not copied into the repo.
+- The cursor-agent cell cleanup ("clean /tmp/.cursor/<slug> after each cell") is an instruction from Bobby; I found no file showing it done.
+
+## Not run
+Nothing was re-run for this summary; no model calls, no gates. It is a reading of the files above.
-- 
